<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-David Jones first quarter sales fall.</title>
<headline>RTRS-David Jones first quarter sales fall.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retailer David Jones Ltd said on Monday that its sales in the 1996/97 first quarter fell 2.9 percent from a year earlier to A$310.5 million.  </p>
<p>Citing lower sales, the company said that its estimated operating profit in the first three months of the current financial year was lower than the year ago level.</p>
<p>It said sales on a like-for-like basis were 4.4 percent lower than in the 1995/96 first quarter.</p>
<p>Trading during the latest period reflected a continuation of the difficuilt retail environment in the fourth quarter of 1995/96, the upmarket retailer said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
